  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-ZWE126</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity for protection of vulnerable workers in line with international labour standards</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This CPO integrates four (5) streams of work aimed at protecting workers and children against unacceptable forms of work. The work will contribute results towards: (i) reducing the impact of HIV and AIDS through workplace policies and programmes, (ii) promoting OSH at work (iii) elimination of child labour and (iv) ending violence and harassment in the world of work (v) developing laws, policies and measures to improve labour rights and working conditions of care workers, including domestic workers. Work is also built from a study on the Inclusion of Persons with Disabilities in Workplace Policies and Programmes on Violence and Harassment (including SGBV) which was conducted in the 2020-2021 biennia and an Action Plan was developed. The specific objective is to strengthen the capacity of employers and workers&#x2019; and their organisations to develop and implement sector specific and enterprise level policies and programmes to address violence and harassment in the world of work. The work also covers the informal sector players that included: Small-scale mining; Cross-border traders; Vendors; Public transport workers; Sex workers; Small-scale farmers and farm workers; Construction; and Manufacturing sector workers.</narrative>
  </description>
